WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.056 --> 00:00:08.919
It's early morning in the African desert.

2
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:14.956
Most of the meerkats are still asleep in their burrow.

3
00:00:14.957 --> 00:00:18.207
But Max is awake.

4
00:00:18.208 --> 00:00:20.553
"I'm hungry!"

5
00:00:20.554 --> 00:00:24.488
His big sister, Zara, opens one eye.

6
00:00:24.489 --> 00:00:29.335
"Shh!" she whispers. "Go back to sleep!"

7
00:00:29.336 --> 00:00:33.188
Max's little brother, Stripe, yawns.

8
00:00:33.189 --> 00:00:36.508
"Is it time to get up?"

9
00:00:36.509 --> 00:00:41.369
Max grins. "I'm going hunting!"

10
00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:45.477
"Meerkats don't hunt alone," Zara says.

11
00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:50.128
"Besides, Mom still has to catch scorpions for you."

12
00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:54.954
"I can catch a scorpion by myself," Max says.

13
00:00:54.955 --> 00:00:59.024
Zara rolls over. "Whatever."

14
00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:03.818
"I'll show her!" Max thinks.

15
00:01:03.819 --> 00:01:07.137
He sneaks to the burrow entrance.

16
00:01:07.138 --> 00:01:14.852
Max steps outside and sniffs the ground.

17
00:01:14.853 --> 00:01:20.977
"No bugs here . . ." Max thinks.

18
00:01:20.978 --> 00:01:26.417
He wanders farther into the warm desert.

19
00:01:26.418 --> 00:01:28.487
He sniffs again.

20
00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:34.772
"This is fun," he thinks. "I'm hunting by myself."

21
00:01:34.773 --> 00:01:37.798
Finally he smells something.

22
00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:42.941
He digs up a tiny worm. "Yum!"

23
00:01:42.942 --> 00:01:45.681
But Max is still hungry.

24
00:01:45.682 --> 00:01:48.860
Suddenly—

25
00:01:48.861 --> 00:01:55.487
screech! Max looks up. "A goshawk!"

26
00:01:55.488 --> 00:01:59.260
He sees a bolt-hole and takes off.

27
00:01:59.261 --> 00:02:02.753
The bird dives after him!

28
00:02:02.754 --> 00:02:06.372
But Max leaps inside just in time!

29
00:02:06.373 --> 00:02:13.650
Max gulps. "That was close.

30
00:02:13.651 --> 00:02:16.220
Maybe Zara was right."

31
00:02:16.221 --> 00:02:21.669
When the hawk is gone, Max decides to go home.

32
00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:25.852
Outside the bolt-hole, Max freezes.

33
00:02:25.853 --> 00:02:31.376
Hisss! A cobra rises in front of him!

34
00:02:31.377 --> 00:02:35.338
It swings its head, ready to strike.

35
00:02:35.339 --> 00:02:38.169
Max jumps out of the way.

36
00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:41.965
"Chee-chee-chee!" he calls.

37
00:02:41.966 --> 00:02:45.062
Stomp! Stomp! Stomp!

38
00:02:45.063 --> 00:02:48.721
The meerkat mob rushes over.

39
00:02:48.722 --> 00:02:52.804
Their fur puffs up as they surround the snake.

40
00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:58.406
They growl and hiss.

41
00:02:58.407 --> 00:03:02.007
The snake slithers off fast.

42
00:03:02.008 --> 00:03:09.601
Mom frowns at Max. "You can't go out by yourself."

43
00:03:09.602 --> 00:03:14.809
"I told you meerkats don't hunt alone," Zara says.

44
00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:19.327
"But I was really hungry," Max says.

45
00:03:19.328 --> 00:03:26.931
Mom sighs. "The mob has to stick together.

46
00:03:26.932 --> 00:03:31.362
That's how we survive."

47
00:03:31.363 --> 00:03:38.508
"Okay," Max says. "Since we're all here . . .

48
00:03:38.509 --> 00:03:43.395
Can we go hunting now?"

